@using MudBlazor

<div class="d-flex flex-column">
    <div class="pa-3" style="max-height:70vh; overflow-y:auto">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="font-weight-bold mb-2">What you rank</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-3">
            Each card is a <b>Portfolio Epic</b> or a <b>Business Outcome</b>, depending on the ART's
            Prioritization setting. A card lists the features of this ART's teams that belong to it; in a PI that
            includes the features the PI's label rule adds to the team boards. Features without a parent are collected in a <i>No Portfolio Epic</i> or <i>No Business Outcome</i> card,
            which you rank like the others.
        </MudText>

        <MudDivider Class="my-3" />

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="font-weight-bold mb-2">General order and PI orders</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            <b>General</b> is the ART's main order. It holds every card with features in the current or a future
            PI (or without a PI), plus the cards you added by hand. Every PI follows the general order unless
            it has its own order.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            Choose a PI to see the order its team boards use. A PI that follows the general order is shown
            read-only: use <b>Edit general order</b>, or <b>Create PI order</b> to give that PI its own order.
            A PI with its own order shows cards that are not in it yet (new features, or cards from the general
            order) as <i>New</i>; Save keeps them. <b>Use general order</b> deletes the PI's own order, and the PI
            follows the general order again.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-3">
            Locked PIs never change by accident: when you save the general order, every locked PI with features
            on this ART's teams that follows it, or has no order yet, first gets its current order saved as its
            own order. A locked PI without any order gets all its cards above the line, in Jira key order.
            Editing a locked PI needs the <i>Edit locked PI</i> right.
        </MudText>

        <MudDivider Class="my-3" />

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="font-weight-bold mb-2">Numbering and moving cards</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            The cards are numbered in one sequence: above the line 1, 2, 3 …, then the line, then the cards
            below it. Type a number in a card's <b>Ranking</b> field and press Enter (or leave the field) to move
            the card there; it stays on its own side of the line. The arrows move a card one place.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-3">
            The square button moves a card across the line: below the line it becomes the first card under the
            line, above the line it becomes the last card above it. Changes are kept only when you <b>Save</b>.
        </MudText>

        <MudDivider Class="my-3" />

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="font-weight-bold mb-2">The line and the team boards</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">
            The team boards of this ART use this order as their default order and show each feature's
            <i>ART #</i> rank. A card below the line takes its features out of the capacity of every team board
            of this ART: they show <i>Below the ART line</i> there.
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-3">
            A team that belongs to several ARTs follows the line of each of them. Its default order comes from
            the ART that has its own order for that PI. If none has one, it comes from the ART whose general
            order applies. When two ARTs tie, the feature Ranking decides.
        </MudText>

        <MudDivider Class="my-3" />

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="font-weight-bold mb-2">Add and Remove</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-3">
            <b>Add</b> puts a Portfolio Epic or Business Outcome without features in this order on the list, at the
            end of the above-the-line group. Cards without features in the order can be removed with the
            <b>X</b> button. Cards with features stay; move them below the line instead. In a PI's own order, a
            card without features that is in the general order comes back from there, so remove it from the
            general order or move it below the line.
        </MudText>

        <MudDivider Class="my-3" />

        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" Class="font-weight-bold mb-2">Excel</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">
            <b>Export</b> downloads the list as it is on the page, with its Ranking, line, Jira ID and summary.
            Change the Ranking numbers and <b>Upload</b> the file: a preview shows what moves, and Apply puts the
            new order on the page as unsaved changes. Upload never adds or removes cards and never moves a card
            across the line. Uploading into a PI that follows the general order creates that PI's own order.
        </MudText>
    </div>
</div>
